Package: ros-desktop-base
Version: @VERSION@
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: ros-branding (= @VERSION@), ros-agent (= @VERSION@),
 gnome-core, gdm3, gnome-control-center, gnome-tweaks, dconf-cli,
 gnome-shell-extension-dashtodock, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator,
 fonts-inter, fonts-noto-core, network-manager-gnome
Recommends: firefox-esr, libreoffice-writer, libreoffice-calc, libreoffice-impress,
 cups, system-config-printer, simple-scan, flatpak
Maintainer: ROS Project <yvesm189@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/yvesm189/ros
Description: ROS desktop (metapackage)
 Pulls in everything that makes a Debian system a ROS workstation: the GNOME
 desktop, the ROS identity and default policy, and the management agent.
 .
 Installing this package on an existing Debian 13 system is the supported way
 to try ROS without building an image.
